---
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/retro-theme.css';
import '@fontsource/bodoni-moda/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/bodoni-moda/latin-400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/bodoni-moda/latin-600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/latin-500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/latin-400.css';
import '../styles/typography.css';
import '../styles/motion.css';
import AndersonLocalization from '../components/AndersonLocalization.astro';
import RVBResonance from '../components/RVBResonance.astro';
import SpinWave from '../components/SpinWave.astro';
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import raven from '../../public/brand/raven-orbit.png';
import displayFont from '@fontsource/bodoni-moda/files/bodoni-moda-latin-600-normal.woff2?url';
const favicon = await getImage({ src: raven, width: 64, format: 'png' });
const pageTitle = 'P. W. Zhao — A few questions about quantum matter';
const pageDescription = 'Pengwei Zhao, theoretical condensed matter physics at HKUST. Topology, disorder, frustrated magnets, and a recent interest in quantum geometry.';
const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
const socialImageURL = new URL('/social/profile-card-v1.png', Astro.site);
const socialImageAlt = 'P. W. Zhao — Hello from Hilbert space. Blue raven and orbital-ring emblem on a peach and mint academic folio.';
import { publications, profile } from '../data/publications';
const journalCount = publications.filter(p => p.kind === 'journal').length;
const preprintCount = publications.length - journalCount;
const topics = [
 { id:'geometry', num:'01', title:'Topology & disorder', subtitle:'When waves refuse to wander.', text:'Disorder can stop a quantum wave from spreading. I study how topology changes that story, especially in chiral symmetry classes. Berry phases, vortices, and unexpected connections to superconductors keep turning up along the way. More recently, I’ve been exploring how quantum geometry affects the behaviour of quantum matter.', tags:'ANDERSON TRANSITIONS / BERRY PHASES', image:'topology-disorder-art.svg', imageAlt:'A wavefunction envelope above a bond-disordered lattice, with a phase-winding inset.', caption:'Anderson localization.', link:'https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.133.226601', linkText:'Topology and the Anderson transition' },
 { id:'disorder', num:'02', title:'Quantum spin liquids', subtitle:'Spins that won’t settle down.', text:'Frustrated magnets can avoid ordinary magnetic order and form quantum spin liquids. I study their emergent excitations, from electric monopoles in Ce-based pyrochlores to spinons and visons in kagome systems, and ask how we might recognize them in experiments. The word “liquid” is not a promise that you can pour one.', tags:'SPIN LIQUIDS / EMERGENT GAUGE FIELDS', image:'quantum-spin-liquids.svg', imageAlt:'A kagome lattice with alternate resonating bond configurations and spinon and vison excitations.', caption:'Resonating singlets on a kagome lattice.', link:'https://doi.org/10.21468/SciPostPhys.19.2.040', linkText:'Topological order in kagome dipolar systems' },
 { id:'collective', num:'03', title:'Correlated matter', subtitle:'Spins, orbitals, and their neighbours.', text:'In a Mott insulator, charges may be stuck, but there is still plenty going on. I study how spins, orbitals, and lattice motion affect one another, from electric polarization driven by multipolar order to topological mechanical boundary modes. Deciding which moving parts can safely be ignored is part of the job.', tags:'MULTIPOLAR ORDER / SPIN–LATTICE COUPLING', image:'correlated-matter.svg', imageAlt:'Spins on a frustrated lattice with reference and displaced atomic positions and displacement vectors.', caption:'A collective spin wave.', link:'https://doi.org/10.1103/pm3h-pz2p', linkText:'Multipolar ferroelectricity in the Mott regime' },
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta name="robots" content={import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_INDEXABLE === 'true' ? 'index,follow' : 'noindex,nofollow'} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="P. W. Zhao" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_GB" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={pageTitle} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={socialImageURL} />
    <meta property="og:image:secure_url" content={socialImageURL} />
    <meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content={socialImageAlt} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={pageTitle} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={socialImageURL} />
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content={socialImageAlt} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href={favicon.src} />
    <link rel="preload" href={displayFont} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="reading-progress" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="page-frame">
      <header class="header">
        <a class="identity" href="#" aria-label="P. W. Zhao home"><Image class="brand-logo" src={raven} width={48} height={48} densities={[1,2]} format="webp" quality={85} loading="eager" alt="" /><span>PWZ<span class="identity-dot">.</span></span></a>
        <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#research">Research <span>01</span></a>
          <a href="#publications">Publications <span>02</span></a>
          <a href="#about">About <span>03</span></a>
        </nav>
        <a class="contact-button" href="#contact">Say hello <span>↗</span></a>
      </header>
      <main id="main">
        <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <div class="hero-eyebrow"><span><i></i> THEORETICAL CONDENSED MATTER PHYSICS</span><span class="prototype-tag">HKUST / HONG KONG</span></div>
          <h1 id="hero-title"><span class="hero-name">P. W. ZHAO</span><Image class="title-logo" src={raven} width={224} height={224} densities={[1,2]} format="webp" quality={85} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" alt="" /></h1>
          <div class="hero-bottom">
            <div class="hero-copy">
              <p class="micro">A THEORIST’S CORNER OF THE INTERNET</p>
              <h2>Hello from<br /><em>Hilbert space.</em></h2>
              <p class="intro">I’m Pengwei Zhao. I do theoretical condensed matter physics at HKUST, mostly on topology, disorder, and frustrated magnets. Lately, I’ve also been thinking about quantum geometry.</p>
              <a class="primary-link" href="#research">Here’s what I work on <span>↘</span></a>
              <div class="hero-footnote profile-links"><a href={profile.scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOOGLE SCHOLAR ↗</a><a href={profile.orcid} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ORCID ↗</a></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="artwork" aria-label="Berry curvature of the lowest Harper–Hofstadter band at flux two fifths">
              <div class="art-top"><span>FIG. 001 / HARPER–HOFSTADTER</span><span class="chern-number">|C| = 2</span></div>
              <canvas id="quantum-art" aria-label="The magnetic Brillouin torus of the Harper–Hofstadter model at flux 2/5, lowest band. Surface color encodes Berry-curvature magnitude, from pale mint for weak curvature to coral and copper red for peaks. All curvature has the same negative sign in the stated convention. Surface height also encodes curvature magnitude as an outward relief from the underlying torus."></canvas>
              <div class="art-bottom"><span>BERRY CURVATURE · Φ/Φ₀ = 2/5</span><button id="motion-toggle" aria-pressed="true"><span class="motion-dot"></span> MOTION ON</button></div>
              <figcaption class="sr-only">A calculated Harper–Hofstadter lowest-band texture. The torus angles are magnetic Bloch momenta u=5kx and v=ky. Color and outward surface relief share a monotone compressed scale for Berry-curvature magnitude. The data come from a 256 by 256 momentum grid; the Chern number is independently checked by the curvature integral and gauge-invariant lattice links. The torus embedding, metallic illumination, and curvature-height scale are artistic choices.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </section>
        <div class="ribbon" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ribbon-track">{[0,1].map(() => <div class="ribbon-group"><span>QUANTUM MATTER</span><b>✳</b><span>TOPOLOGY</span><b>✳</b><span>LOCALIZATION</span><b>✳</b><span>SPIN LIQUIDS</span><b>✳</b></div>)}</div></div>
        <section id="research" class="research-section section-pad">
          <div class="section-heading"><p class="micro">01 / WHAT I WORK ON</p><span class="micro aside-label">CURRENT PREOCCUPATIONS</span></div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Questions I<br /><em>keep coming back to.</em></h2>
          <div class="research-layout">
            <div class="topic-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Research directions" aria-orientation="vertical">
              {topics.map((topic, index) => <button role="tab" id={`tab-${topic.id}`} aria-controls={`panel-${topic.id}`} aria-selected={index===0 ? 'true':'false'} tabindex={index===0 ? 0 : -1} data-topic={topic.id} class={index===0?'topic active':'topic'}><span class="topic-num">{topic.num}</span><span>{topic.title}</span><span class="topic-arrow">↗</span></button>)}
              <p class="section-note">Three recurring themes.<br />Occasionally, the same problem in disguise.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="topic-panels">
              {topics.map((topic,index)=><article role="tabpanel" id={`panel-${topic.id}`} aria-labelledby={`tab-${topic.id}`} tabindex="0" hidden={index!==0}>
                <figure class="research-figure"><div class="research-image">{topic.id === 'disorder' ? <RVBResonance /> : topic.id === 'collective' ? <SpinWave /> : <AndersonLocalization />}</div><figcaption>{topic.caption}<span>{topic.id === 'geometry' ? 'Model visualization' : 'Conceptual schematic'}</span></figcaption></figure>
                <p class="micro topic-tags">{topic.tags}</p><h3>{topic.subtitle}</h3><p class="topic-description">{topic.text}</p><a class="research-paper-link" href={topic.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{topic.linkText} <span>↗</span></a>
              </article>)}
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="publications" class="publications-section section-pad">
          <div class="section-heading"><p class="micro">02 / PUBLICATIONS & PREPRINTS</p><a class="micro aside-label scholar-link" href={profile.scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOOGLE SCHOLAR ↗</a></div>
          <div class="publications-heading"><h2 class="section-title">The paper trail<span>.</span></h2><a class="bibliography-link" href="/publications.bib" download="pengwei-zhao.bib">BIBTEX ↓</a></div>
          <p class="publication-intro">Topology, disorder, and emergent phenomena in quantum matter.</p>
          <div class="publication-controls" role="group" aria-label="Filter publications">
            <button class="publication-filter active" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true" aria-controls="publication-list">All work <span>{publications.length}</span></button>
            <button class="publication-filter" data-filter="journal" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="publication-list">Journal articles <span>{journalCount}</span></button>
            <button class="publication-filter" data-filter="preprint" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="publication-list">Preprints <span>{preprintCount}</span></button>
          </div>
          <p class="sr-only" id="publication-count" aria-live="polite">{publications.length} works shown</p>
          <div id="publication-list">
            {publications.map((paper, index) => <article class="publication-entry" id={paper.id} data-kind={paper.kind}>
              <div class="paper-index"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span>{paper.year}</span></div>
              <div class="paper-main">
                <p class="micro paper-category">{paper.topic} <span class:list={['publication-status', { preprint: paper.kind === 'preprint' }]}>{paper.kind === 'journal' ? 'JOURNAL ARTICLE' : 'PREPRINT'}</span></p>
                <h3><a href={paper.doi ? `https://doi.org/${paper.doi}` : `https://arxiv.org/abs/${paper.arxiv}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{paper.title}</a></h3>
                <p class="paper-authors">{paper.authors.map((author, i) => <span>{i > 0 && ', '}{author === profile.fullName ? <strong>{author}</strong> : author}</span>)}</p>
                <p class="paper-venue">{paper.kind === 'journal' ? <><em>{paper.journal}</em> <strong>{paper.volume}</strong>, {paper.pages} ({paper.year})</> : <>arXiv:{paper.arxiv} ({paper.year}){paper.revised && <span class="revision-note"> · Revised {paper.revised}</span>}</>}</p>
                <div class="publication-links">
                  {paper.doi && <a href={`https://doi.org/${paper.doi}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Journal article: ${paper.title}`}>DOI ↗</a>}
                  <a href={`https://arxiv.org/abs/${paper.arxiv}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`arXiv: ${paper.title}`}>arXiv ↗</a>
                  <a href={`https://arxiv.org/pdf/${paper.arxiv}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Read PDF: ${paper.title}`}>PDF ↗</a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>)}
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="about" class="about-section section-pad">
          <div class="section-heading"><p class="micro">03 / ABOUT</p><span class="micro">ABOUT</span></div>
          <div class="about-layout"><div class="about-symbol" aria-hidden="true">ψ<span>(r)</span></div><div><p class="micro about-name">PENGWEI ZHAO / 赵鹏威</p><h2>A bit of<br /><em>background.</em></h2><p>After completing my PhD in Physics at Peking University, I continued my research at HKUST. The work focuses on topology, disorder, and frustrated magnets.</p><p>These topics often overlap. An idea that helps with one problem can turn out to be useful in another. Finding those connections is one of the things I enjoy about doing theory.</p><div class="about-profile-links"><a class="text-link" href={profile.orcid} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ORCID <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={profile.scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div>
        </section>
        <footer id="contact" class="footer">
          <div class="footer-top"><p>Let’s compare<br /><em>notes.</em></p><div class="contact-details"><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`} class="footer-contact">{profile.email} <span>↗</span></a><p>Questions, ideas, or a well-aimed objection are all welcome.</p><p>Department of Physics<br />The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology</p></div></div>
          <div class="footer-bottom"><a class="identity" href="#"><Image class="brand-logo" src={raven} width={48} height={48} densities={[1,2]} format="webp" quality={85} loading="eager" alt="" />PWZ.</a><span>© 2026 P. W. ZHAO</span><a href="#">BACK TO THE TOP ↑</a></div>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>

    <script>
      import "../../public/motion.js";
      import "../../public/interactions.js";
      import "../../public/visualizations.js";
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
